WEBVTT

00:00:06.073 --> 00:00:08.913
-The engine from the photo.
-It's a perfect match.

00:00:09.033 --> 00:00:11.593
How did the tow truck figure it out?

00:00:11.633 --> 00:00:14.953
It's official. You're coming to
all my races from now on.

00:00:15.033 --> 00:00:17.033
Now you're talkin'!

00:00:18.353 --> 00:00:19.793
(FANFARE)

00:00:20.353 --> 00:00:22.273
Hyeeugh!

00:00:22.353 --> 00:00:24.353
(GARBLED NOISES)

00:00:25.433 --> 00:00:27.713
Mater, let's go. You're on.

00:00:32.113 --> 00:00:34.433
Your Majesty, may I present

00:00:34.473 --> 00:00:38.473
for the investiture of honorary
knighthood of the British Realm...

00:00:38.593 --> 00:00:42.073
Tow Mater of Radiator Springs.

00:00:42.113 --> 00:00:44.113
Go get 'em, buddy.

00:00:48.113 --> 00:00:50.113
(WHIRRING)

00:00:51.793 --> 00:00:56.553
I hereby dub thee Sir Tow Mater.

00:00:56.673 --> 00:00:58.073
(CHEERING)

00:00:58.113 --> 00:01:01.473
Sir? Shoot, you can just call me Mater,
Your Majesty.

00:01:01.513 --> 00:01:03.793
I don't wanna hear none of this "sir"
business.

00:01:03.873 --> 00:01:05.913
By the way, have y'all met each other?

00:01:05.953 --> 00:01:07.753
Queen, McQueen. McQueen, Queen.

00:01:07.833 --> 00:01:09.793
McQueen, McMissile. McMissile,
McQueen. Queen, McMissile.

00:01:14.153 --> 00:01:15.633
(HORNS HONK)

00:01:15.713 --> 00:01:18.753
MATER: So there we was,
my rocket jets going full blast,

00:01:18.833 --> 00:01:20.833
McQueen hanging on for dear life

00:01:20.913 --> 00:01:24.833
when suddenly them two nasty lemons
come out of nowheres, guns drawed.

00:01:24.993 --> 00:01:26.713
We was goners.

00:01:26.793 --> 00:01:29.993
But then, out of nowhere
this beautiful spy car

00:01:30.033 --> 00:01:32.033
swoops in from the sky to save us!

00:01:32.153 --> 00:01:35.113
That's a very entertaining story,
young man.

00:01:35.153 --> 00:01:37.153
Oh, Minny, please. Come on!

00:01:37.193 --> 00:01:41.033
None of this happened.
Rocket jets, flying spy cars.

00:01:41.153 --> 00:01:44.673
No, you're quite right.
It does sound a bit far-fetched.

00:01:44.753 --> 00:01:46.593
Holley! What are you doin' here?

00:01:46.673 --> 00:01:49.593
Hello, Mater!
It's so good to see you again.

00:01:49.673 --> 00:01:50.673
Finn!

00:01:50.713 --> 00:01:52.833
Our satellites picked up
an urgent communiqué.

00:01:53.033 --> 00:01:54.713
So you got-a my email.

00:01:54.793 --> 00:01:57.233
Y'all is going to have a great time!

00:01:57.353 --> 00:02:01.193
Everybody, this here's Finn McMissile.
He's a secret agent.

00:02:01.273 --> 00:02:02.433
Don't tell nobody.

00:02:02.513 --> 00:02:04.513
And this is Holley Shiftwell.

00:02:04.593 --> 00:02:06.593
-She's...
-I'm Mater's girlfriend.

00:02:06.713 --> 00:02:08.673
It's so nice to meet you all.

00:02:08.753 --> 00:02:10.953
-(CLANG)
-Guido believe you now.

00:02:11.033 --> 00:02:13.673
Whoa, honey.
You got a nasty dent there.

00:02:13.753 --> 00:02:15.593
-Yeah.
-Was that from when you swooped in

00:02:15.673 --> 00:02:17.513
and you saved them in London?

00:02:17.593 --> 00:02:19.593
-Van!
-What? I'm just asking!

00:02:19.673 --> 00:02:24.393
Don't you worry. My baby Ramone
can get that fixed up for you in no time.

00:02:24.433 --> 00:02:27.513
Yeah, sure thing.
No problemo. Let me go get my tools.

00:02:27.593 --> 00:02:30.393
Oh, no. I'm keeping that dent.
It's way too valuable.

00:02:31.633 --> 00:02:35.873
A valuable dent?
She's as crazy as Mater.

00:02:35.873 --> 00:02:37.713
Those two are perfect for each other.

00:02:37.793 --> 00:02:40.313
There's one thing I still don't get.

00:02:40.393 --> 00:02:43.233
The bad guys hit me with the beam
from the camera, right?

00:02:43.313 --> 00:02:46.993
-So, why didn't I...
-Explode in a fiery inferno?

00:02:47.073 --> 00:02:49.233
-Yeah.
-We couldn't figure that out, either.

00:02:49.273 --> 00:02:52.313
Our investigation proved
that allinol was actually gasoline

00:02:52.393 --> 00:02:55.753
and Axlerod engineered it so when it
got hit by the beam, it would explode.

00:02:55.833 --> 00:02:59.913
Wait a second, Fillmore.
You said my fuel was safe!

00:03:02.433 --> 00:03:07.513
If you're implying that I switched
that rot-gut excuse for alternative fuel

00:03:07.593 --> 00:03:11.473
with my all-natural, sustainable,
organic biofuel

00:03:11.553 --> 00:03:16.913
just because I never trusted Axlerod,
you're dead wrong, man!

00:03:17.033 --> 00:03:19.113
It was him!

00:03:19.153 --> 00:03:23.233
Once big oil, always big oil, man.

00:03:23.273 --> 00:03:24.753
Tree-hugger.

00:03:25.593 --> 00:03:29.153
The Radiator Springs Grand Prix
is about to begin.

00:03:29.273 --> 00:03:31.553
All spectators, clear the starting line.

00:03:34.433 --> 00:03:36.953
I can't wait to get rockin'.
This is gonna be wicked!

00:03:37.033 --> 00:03:38.673
We should do this every year.

00:03:38.753 --> 00:03:41.873
Yeah, I just figured we never found out
who the world's fastest car is.

00:03:41.953 --> 00:03:44.513
Plus, no press, no trophy, just racing.

00:03:44.593 --> 00:03:48.193
-The way I like it.
-Francesco likes it like this, too.

00:03:48.313 --> 00:03:51.873
-Francesco, I'd like you to meet...
-Signorina Sally.

00:03:51.953 --> 00:03:53.313
It is official.

00:03:53.393 --> 00:03:55.953
Lightning McQueen
is the luckiest car in the world.

00:03:56.073 --> 00:03:58.153
Why, thank you.

00:03:58.273 --> 00:04:01.353
Which he will have to be to have
a chance against Francesco today!

00:04:01.473 --> 00:04:04.513
See you at the finish line, Mc...
What is that?

00:04:04.753 --> 00:04:07.113
Just something I had made up
for the occasion.

00:04:07.473 --> 00:04:09.473
Is-a good, McQueen. Very funny.

00:04:09.513 --> 00:04:12.353
Was-a funnier when I did it,
but it's-a very funny.

00:04:12.473 --> 00:04:15.713
What are you going to do next?
Are you going to take off your fenders?

00:04:15.793 --> 00:04:17.473
Try it. You'll like it.

00:04:17.593 --> 00:04:19.793
So, he's not so good-looking.

00:04:19.873 --> 00:04:22.193
-Yeah. Nice try.
-I'm serious!

00:04:22.353 --> 00:04:24.553
That's why I love you, Sally.

00:04:24.633 --> 00:04:27.433
-Wish me luck!
-You don't need it!

00:04:27.513 --> 00:04:31.353
Ooh-hm!
That Francesco is fine-looking!

00:04:31.433 --> 00:04:32.993
And those open wheels.

00:04:33.073 --> 00:04:36.113
Ooh, I'm gonna have to go get myself
some coolant.

00:04:36.993 --> 00:04:39.033
(ENGINES REV)

00:04:47.513 --> 00:04:48.673
Go, Lightning!

00:05:07.233 --> 00:05:08.873
-Go, Stickers!
-Right on, man!

00:05:08.953 --> 00:05:10.913
-Go get 'em, tiger!
-Bravo, bravo!

00:05:10.993 --> 00:05:14.393
-Go, Lightning, go!
-Go, McQueen! Whoo-hoo!

00:05:14.433 --> 00:05:16.873
-(BLEEPING)
-Finn? Time to go.

00:05:16.953 --> 00:05:19.233
Siddeley's gassed, geared
and ready to fly.

00:05:20.073 --> 00:05:23.233
-You're leavin' already?
-We've got another mission.

00:05:23.353 --> 00:05:25.673
Just stopped by here
to pick something up.

00:05:26.753 --> 00:05:30.473
Somethin' tells me you're not
talkin' about souvenir bumper stickers.

00:05:30.553 --> 00:05:32.953
Her Majesty asked for you personally,
Mater.

00:05:33.033 --> 00:05:36.393
-But I told y'all before, I'm not a spy.
-We know.

00:05:36.433 --> 00:05:40.153
Spy or not, you're still the smartest,
most honest chap we've ever met.

00:05:40.233 --> 00:05:43.633
-Don't forget massively charming.
-Well, thanks.

00:05:43.713 --> 00:05:46.833
But as much fun as it was
hangin' with y'all, this...

00:05:46.913 --> 00:05:49.593
-(ALL SHOUT EXCITEDLY)
-This is home.

00:05:49.673 --> 00:05:52.593
That's all right. We understand.
But I'll be back.

00:05:52.633 --> 00:05:54.513
You still owe me that first date.

00:05:54.593 --> 00:05:57.593
If there's ever anything I can do for you,
just let me know.

00:05:57.673 --> 00:05:59.913
Well, I sure appreciate that. Thank you.

00:06:01.273 --> 00:06:04.033
Actually, there is one thing.

00:06:04.513 --> 00:06:06.833
Whoo-hoo! (LAUGHS)

00:06:06.953 --> 00:06:08.913
Whoo! I'll be doggone!

00:06:08.993 --> 00:06:10.513
(SIGHS AND GASPS)

00:06:13.633 --> 00:06:15.113
Whoa, whoa, whoa!

00:06:18.113 --> 00:06:19.673
Thanks, Mater!

00:06:27.113 --> 00:06:29.113
Ha-ha-ha! Whoo!

00:06:30.873 --> 00:06:32.753
Impossible!

00:06:33.313 --> 00:06:34.753
-Ha-ha!
-Mater!

00:06:34.833 --> 00:06:37.473
Check it out.
They let me keep the rockets.

00:06:37.513 --> 00:06:39.633
I'll see you at the finish line, buddy!

00:06:39.713 --> 00:06:41.673
Not if I see you first!

00:06:41.753 --> 00:06:43.753
Yippee!

